kled_duck","wikidataId":"Q382321"}},{"commonNames":[],"ottId":1041429,"scientificName":"Cuculus","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Cuculus is a genus of cuckoos which has representatives in most of the Old World, although the greatest diversity is in tropical southern and southeastern Asia.","revisionId":1365286362,"title":"Cuculus","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuculus","wikidataId":"Q746658"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Large Black-headed Gulls and allies","source":"Catalogue of Life"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Ichthyaetus","confidence":94,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Ichthyaetus Kaup, 1829","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":7237184},"ottId":1044949,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Ichthyaetus","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Ichthyaetus is a genus of gulls in the order Charadriiformes. The genus name comes from Ancient Greek ἰχθύς (ikhthús), meaning \"fish\", and ἀετός (aetós), meaning \"eagle\", and thus, \"fish eagle\".","revisionId":1363219631,"title":"Ichthyaetus","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ichthyaetus","wikidataId":"Q639312"}},{"commonNames":[],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Totanus","confidence":94,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Totanus Cuvier, 1800","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":4849718},"ottId":3596885,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Totanus","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Totanus (Bechstein, 1803) is a generic name previously applied to various waders or shorebirds, now subsumed within Tringa. Created by Johann Matthäus Bechstein, it derives from the species name for the common redshank, described by Carl Linnaeus in his landmark 1758 10th edition of Systema Naturae as Scolopax totanus, from totano, the Italian name for the bird.","revisionId":1008857211,"title":"Totanus","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Totanus","wikidataId":"Q7828263"}},{"commonNames":[],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Dynamopterus","confidence":94,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Dynamopterus Milne-Edwards, 1892","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKe